{
  "summary": "Passes base32 I2P addresses directly to the SAM bridge `STREAM CONNECT` command rather than issuing a preliminary `NAMING LOOKUP` command. This eliminates a round trip to the local SAM bridge on every outbound I2P connection.",
  "problem": "Outbound I2P connections perform a redundant `NAMING LOOKUP` step that adds latency. Furthermore, when unresolvable peers cause the lookup to return an empty `VALUE=` key, Bitcoin Core treats it as an internal proxy error rather than a peer reachability failure, preventing AddrMan from recording the failed attempt.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description quotes the SAM v3 API specification stating that STREAM CONNECT accepts `.b32.i2p` as DESTINATION (https://i2p.net/en/docs/api/samv3/#sam-virtual-streams-connect)",
    "PR description notes minimum router versions supporting this (Java I2P 0.9.48, i2pd 2.38.0) are older than encryption type requirements already merged in #35696"
  ],
